        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Maybe I'm mis-remembering but I didn't think he needed three groups of 55th level... although maybe I was thinking of facing him with one group of ~60s... the name is familiar but it's been so long I can't reliably remember (I think he's a ghost? --- Oh, wait, he spawns AFTER one of those black reavers dies? After spawning multiple black reavers? And he has a fire AE that destroys most in two pulses? Or that may be some one else...)</P><P>Brax, the clueless <img src=icon_smile_tongue.gif border=0 align=middle></P><P>EDIT: Since it's not the ROGUE epic quest I only know what little bit of info I picked up between handing out Halas 10lb Meat Pies and being told to "go poke that"... but the more I think about it... Lord G ~may~ just spawn from GENERAL Black Reavers and is kill-able ---- I seem to remember whacking some black reavers outside the castle with the locked door, in that area surrounded by water, before you get on the bridge with the neat little gazeboes.</P><P>Anyway, I seem to remember that after a few black reaver spawns we got Lord G to pop and whacked him pretty easy. I -think-.  There was some OTHER ghostly guy who spawned INSIDE the castle with the locked door... and I remember he fired off an AE that knocked off like 2000 hit points or something: I staggered up the stairs toward the invisible ramps and nearly died.  I think he's the one that Standard Wisdom said to send four mage fire pets after him (since they were immune to his fire dot)... </P><P>Of course this was ages ago.  One level 65 mage might be able to sic his pet on the thing. <img src=icon_smile.gif border=0 align=middle></P><P>Good luck in any event!</P><P><BR>Edited by - Braxzana on 10/29/2004  12:05:19<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
